@startuml composite-emission
title US-06: Composite Emission - Atomic supersession: SIGNAL_LOSS marked SUPERSEDED, COMPOSITE inserted

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
database "Redis\nalert-events\n(pub/sub)" as AlertEvents
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

note over Evaluator
  Both signals confirmed (see signal-correlation diagram).
  SIGNAL_LOSS was already emitted when entity went dark.
  Now: supersede it and emit COMPOSITE in one transaction.
end note

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish COMPOSITE alert event\n{ alert_id: $composite_id,\n  alert_type: COMPOSITE, priority: ELEVATED,\n  entity_id: $dark_entity_id,\n  pair_key, episode_start_ms,\n  dark_since_ms, distance_at_detection,\n  supersedes_alert_ids: [$signal_loss_alert_id],\n  location, timestamp_ms }

Kafka -> API : consume COMPOSITE alert

API -> TSDB : BEGIN TRANSACTION\n--\nUPDATE alerts\n  SET status = 'SUPERSEDED',\n      superseded_by = $composite_id\n  WHERE alert_id = $signal_loss_alert_id\n    AND status NOT IN ('SUPERSEDED');\n--\nINSERT INTO alerts\n  (alert_id, entity_id, alert_type, status, detected_at, payload)\n  VALUES ($composite_id, ..., 'COMPOSITE', 'NEW', ...)\n  ON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING;\n--\nCOMMIT

note over TSDB
  Atomic: both the status update and the insert
  succeed or both roll back.
  ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on the INSERT ensures
  Kafka replay is safe — composite row already present
  after the first successful commit.
  superseded_by column is a nullable FK → alerts.alert_id.
end note

TSDB --> API : transaction committed (or idempotent no-op on replay)

API -> AlertEvents : PUBLISH alert-events\n{ type: ALERT_SUPERSEDED,\n  payload: { alert_id: $signal_loss_alert_id,\n    new_status: SUPERSEDED, superseded_by: $composite_id } }

API -> AlertEvents : PUBLISH alert-events\n{ type: ALERT_CREATED,\n  payload: { alert_id: $composite_id,\n    alert_type: COMPOSITE, status: NEW, ... } }

note over API
  Two typed messages on alert-events pub/sub.
  Dashboard can update the existing SIGNAL_LOSS card
  to show SUPERSEDED, then display the new COMPOSITE card.
  Fan-out per connection: scope filter applied before WebSocket push.
end note

API --> Dashboard : push ALERT_SUPERSEDED + ALERT_CREATED\nover WebSocket (scope-matched connections only)

Dashboard --> Operator : SIGNAL_LOSS card updated to SUPERSEDED\nnew COMPOSITE alert displayed at elevated priority\nstatus: NEW

note over Dashboard, Operator
  Operator sees the incident history:
  the original SIGNAL_LOSS is visible as SUPERSEDED
  alongside the COMPOSITE that explains it.
  One active incident, not two.
end note

@enduml
